       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a common starting dose, to titrate up.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If the dose is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it is above the usual maximum.\n\nIf the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide is usually preferred to going higher on amlodipine."
